node_modules/

# dist/ is NOT ignored, and that is deliberate.
#
# The deployment cannot build it. Setting `outputDirectory` in vercel.json --
# which Vercel requires whenever `buildCommand` is set -- puts the Python
# function on a code path that measures 526 MB against a 500 MB ceiling,
# while the same deployment without it measures 291 MB and ships. So the SPA
# is built here, committed, and served by the API process (see
# `src/tscheduler/api/asgi.py`).
#
# Practical consequence: run `npm run build` and commit the result before
# deploying, or the deployed UI is the last one someone remembered to build.
